What:		/proc/uid_cputime/show_uid_perf
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Miru H.40 kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only OnePlus per-task performance-counter snapshot used by the
		Android 14 UID performance-accounting stack. Each task row reports
		command name, PID, TGID, UID, the configured hardware perf-event
		counts, and instruction-count attribution across up to eight cpuset
		groups. Aggregate rows retain counters for tasks that have exited.

		Collection is disabled by default and starts only when userspace sets
		/sys/module/uid_sys_stats/parameters/uid_perf_enable to 1.

What:		/proc/cpuset_info/show_hash
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Miru H.40 kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only mapping from live cpuset cgroup IDs and names to the bounded
		eight-slot accounting indices reported by show_uid_perf.

What:		/proc/cpuset_info/dbg_enable
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Miru H.40 kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read/write diagnostic gate for UID performance cpuset-accounting logs.
		The default value is 0.

What:		/sys/module/uid_sys_stats/parameters/uid_perf_enable
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Miru H.40 kernel maintainers
Description:
		Boolean master switch for per-task hardware performance counters.
		Only 0 and 1 are accepted. The default is 0.

What:		/sys/module/uid_sys_stats/parameters/uid_perf_debug
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Miru H.40 kernel maintainers
Description:
		Boolean diagnostic logging switch for UID performance accounting.

What:		/sys/module/uid_sys_stats/parameters/uid_perf_event_id
What:		/sys/module/uid_sys_stats/parameters/uid_perf_event_type
What:		/sys/module/uid_sys_stats/parameters/uid_perf_event_pin
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	Miru H.40 kernel maintainers
Description:
		Three-element arrays configuring the raw perf-event IDs, perf-event
		types, and pinned flags used by UID performance accounting. Donor
		defaults are event IDs 0x8, 0x11, and 0x24, all PERF_TYPE_RAW and
		unpinned.
